  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Tennessee through FY2027 to date total $1.2B across 884 awards, with an average award size of $1.4M and obligations down 90.4% year over year. The Department of Energy is the largest buying agency in the state, obligating $978M so far in FY2027 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $150M and the Department of Justice at $42.2M. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligation, receiving $803M in FY2027 to date, and Remediation Services and Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing follow at $113M and $68M respectively. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC is the top vendor with $489M in obligations, followed by UT-BATTELLE LLC at $302M and UNITED CLEANUP OAK RIDGE LLC at $113M. Historical obligations show much larger annual totals in prior fiscal years: FY22 through FY26 range from $10.8B to $12.5B, with FY27 currently at $1.2B as a fiscal year to date total.",
    "sections": [
