        "body": "The state has received $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The award count for that period is 884, and the average award size is $1.4M. Obligations are down 90.4% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Tennessee?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy leads buying agencies with $978M in obligations for FY2027 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $150M and the Department of Justice at $42.2M. CONSOLIDATED NUCLEAR SECURITY, LLC is the top vendor with $489M, UT-BATTELLE LLC is second with $302M, and UNITED CLEANUP OAK RIDGE LLC is third with $113M."
      }
    ]
